WEBVTT

00:01.350 --> 00:02.910
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:04.500 --> 00:07.920
This looks like the Labyrinth 
stratum's transfer circle.

00:07.920 --> 00:08.930
Damn it.

00:08.930 --> 00:14.000
There's a strong chance Kerioyl tampered 
with the Origin stratum's transfer circle.

00:14.000 --> 00:17.110
In other words, we've lost control over it.

00:17.400 --> 00:22.380
Yeah. But I don't think his 
side knows who got sent where.

00:22.710 --> 00:27.380
The transfer circle doesn't have enough power 
to return us to Clearflow Lake stratum.

00:27.660 --> 00:30.600
We need to get our hands on a magic 
stone that's charged up with power.

00:31.300 --> 00:34.170
Let's start with going by 
the Hunters Association.

00:34.170 --> 00:35.370
Good idea.

00:35.740 --> 00:37.140
<i>L-ea-v-in m-ea h-ea-r?</i>

00:43.180 --> 00:46.020
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine, I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

00:48.510 --> 00:50.370
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

00:50.370 --> 00:52.310
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

00:52.310 --> 00:57.760
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

00:53.400 --> 00:59.280
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine, I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

00:57.760 --> 01:00.140
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

01:00.140 --> 01:01.940
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

02:16.110 --> 02:19.990
<b>The Animals and the Girl</b>

02:16.340 --> 02:19.000
<i>The place we were sent was 
the Labyrinth stratum.</i>

02:19.480 --> 02:22.990
<i>It's where I fell before, when I 
was involved in a stratum split.</i>

02:25.690 --> 02:28.740
We were getting close to running 
out of preserved foods,

02:28.740 --> 02:31.500
so Boxxo showing up is a great help!

02:31.500 --> 02:38.420
<b>Disaster Relief
Vending Machine</b>

02:31.870 --> 02:35.300
<i>The Labyrinth stratum was having a hard 
time dealing with its own monster assault.</i>

02:35.750 --> 02:39.670
<i>There are actual vending machines that 
don't charge during times of disaster,</i>

02:39.670 --> 02:42.510
<i>so I tried taking a lesson from 
that by vending for free.</i>

02:42.510 --> 02:46.510
Director Labyrinth, have you noticed 
the strangeness that's occurring?

02:46.510 --> 02:50.020
You mean, how the transfer 
circle is inoperable?

02:50.020 --> 02:51.720
Not just that.

02:51.720 --> 02:54.310
There has been a huge outbreak of monsters,

02:54.310 --> 02:59.290
but the one controlling them is the Netherlord,
the Demon Lord's left-arm general.

02:59.290 --> 03:01.910
You mean it's that serious?!

03:01.910 --> 03:05.640
I guess I shouldn't be surprised 
that info hadn't reached me,

03:05.640 --> 03:09.030
when I'm basically the least 
capable of the directors.

03:09.400 --> 03:12.500
I'm definitely not cut out for this job.

03:12.500 --> 03:15.660
<i>This director's kind of pessimistic.</i>

03:15.670 --> 03:17.170
<b>Labyrinth Stratum Hunters Association</b>

03:17.500 --> 03:18.990
We've saved!

03:18.990 --> 03:20.590
This food is great!

03:20.590 --> 03:21.680
I'm so thankful!

03:21.680 --> 03:24.930
<i>Good, everyone seems happy.</i>

03:25.320 --> 03:27.840
I checked to see if they had a 
magic stone at the item shop,

03:27.840 --> 03:29.390
but it seems they're out of stock.

03:29.390 --> 03:30.310
I see.

03:30.310 --> 03:33.820
Well we aren't going anywhere if 
the transfer circle won't work.

03:33.820 --> 03:36.650
I have an idea for how to get a magic stone.

03:36.990 --> 03:40.880
Would you mind making adjustments 
to the transfer circle?

03:42.010 --> 03:43.820
Okay, I'll go do that.

03:44.910 --> 03:47.330
<i>Your co-in there?</i>

03:47.330 --> 03:49.750
You figured me out, Boxxo?

03:49.750 --> 03:52.280
Yes, I plan to go into the labyrinth.

03:55.270 --> 03:56.380
<i>What's that?</i>

03:56.380 --> 03:58.590
<i>D-er-ex-t-er, s-our-ns.</i>

03:59.110 --> 04:01.160
It might be surviving hunters.

04:02.100 --> 04:04.340
<i>Then there's no time to waste.</i>

04:05.340 --> 04:07.000
That's helpful, Boxxo.

04:10.980 --> 04:12.610
I'll assist!

04:12.610 --> 04:13.850
Thank...

04:15.360 --> 04:16.320
...you...

04:18.370 --> 04:21.550
<i>Well, that's how one </i>would<i> react 
if they came across a bear</i>

04:21.550 --> 04:23.730
<i>carrying a cardboard vending machine.</i>

04:24.030 --> 04:26.320
Oh! This one is with me.

04:26.320 --> 04:27.970
As is that one.

04:31.250 --> 04:33.630
Oh, did that change shape?

04:33.630 --> 04:38.500
Details can wait, but just think 
of him as that sort of magic item.

04:38.500 --> 04:39.630
Wow.

04:39.630 --> 04:41.660
Nice to meet you, magic item.

04:41.660 --> 04:42.880
<i>Hello there.</i>

04:42.880 --> 04:45.750
Oh my, he responded.

04:42.880 --> 04:45.760
<b>Kikoyu</b>

04:45.750 --> 04:49.270
Oh, please leave the monsters to these two.

04:52.630 --> 04:54.650
Cover your ears, please!

05:01.760 --> 05:05.280
<i>I think they could have handled 
this just fine without our help.</i>

05:05.280 --> 05:10.150
I've never heard of an unasusu and a 
kirise that can overwhelm monsters.

05:10.150 --> 05:12.370
These two are unique.

05:12.370 --> 05:14.380
They're quite outstanding and kind,

05:14.380 --> 05:16.910
and a certain someone's 
power made them stronger.

05:17.210 --> 05:19.770
<i>A certain someone's power? 
That gets me curious.</i>

05:19.770 --> 05:23.220
I will clean this up, so please be patient.

05:23.670 --> 05:25.280
<i>What's that?</i>

05:30.440 --> 05:32.930
What's that ball of dirt?

05:32.930 --> 05:38.310
I am willing to answer that, but could 
you tell me who the two of you are?

05:38.560 --> 05:40.270
Ah, pardon me.

05:40.270 --> 05:44.560
I am the director of the Hunters 
Association on Clearflow Lake stratum.

05:44.560 --> 05:48.980
This is Boxxo, a magic item 
with a person's soul inside.

05:48.980 --> 05:52.530
With his own sense of self, he's a 
dependable ally who can carry on a conversation.

05:52.530 --> 05:53.710
<i>Hello there.</i>

05:53.900 --> 05:57.200
A person's soul residing 
inside a magic item?

05:57.200 --> 05:59.970
That's a little like that certain someone.

05:59.970 --> 06:02.280
<i>Who could she be talking about?</i>

06:02.720 --> 06:05.770
I will now introduce myself and mine.

06:05.770 --> 06:09.220
I am Kikoyu, and the white unasusu is Botan.

06:09.220 --> 06:11.250
The black kirise is Kuroyata.

06:12.690 --> 06:16.470
<i>Based on what I saw of that battle, 
these two are quite strong.</i>

06:16.920 --> 06:20.720
<i>I wonder if the girl has 
some power of her own.</i>

06:21.000 --> 06:24.410
My powers merely include the ability to 
control a very small amount of cold air

06:24.410 --> 06:27.100
and the ability to move while 
concealing my presence.

06:27.100 --> 06:29.580
<i>Huh. If she can mask her presence,</i>

06:29.580 --> 06:32.490
<i>she could just hide while the 
others deal with combat.</i>

06:32.490 --> 06:34.080
Yes, that is true.

06:34.080 --> 06:37.490
I am always relying on Kuroyata 
and Botan to save me.

06:37.750 --> 06:40.500
<i>I guess that makes her an animal handler.</i>

06:40.500 --> 06:43.150
I am not an animal handler.

06:43.150 --> 06:47.030
They are smart enough to think 
on their own, and comprehend.

06:47.030 --> 06:49.520
I am simply the one who benefits.

06:49.520 --> 06:53.380
Kikoyu. With whom are you speaking?

06:53.380 --> 06:55.490
<i>With me, that's who...</i>

06:55.490 --> 06:59.520
<i>Oh, wait a minute. Was she answering 
me even though I wasn't vocalizing?</i>

06:59.520 --> 07:03.960
I can hear the inner voice 
of whomever I touch.

07:03.960 --> 07:05.030
<i>For real?</i>

07:05.030 --> 07:07.450
Yes, for real.

07:08.210 --> 07:12.780
But it was rude for me to do that 
without permission. I'm sorry.

07:12.780 --> 07:14.040
<i>I-s o-k-a-y.</i>

07:14.280 --> 07:18.240
Um, if you wish,
would could eat while we talk.

07:18.240 --> 07:19.660
Sure, let's do that.

07:19.660 --> 07:21.370
<i>Mealtime means it's my ti—</i>

07:21.370 --> 07:25.720
Then as thanks, I shall provide the food.

07:28.030 --> 07:31.540
<i>She's not about to grow a 
plant right now, is she?</i>

07:35.300 --> 07:36.550
<i>What?!</i>

07:36.550 --> 07:39.170
How in the world does that work?

07:39.500 --> 07:44.330
Not only does this Piece of Field 
absorb monsters as nutrients,

07:44.330 --> 07:49.850
but if you plant and water a seedling, 
it can make it grow rapidly!

07:50.330 --> 07:52.770
<i>Piece of Field?</i>

07:58.310 --> 08:01.490
It will be a short while 
until it finishes cooking,

08:01.490 --> 08:04.520
so I will tell you more about us.

08:05.050 --> 08:10.230
You might find the story difficult 
to believe, but it is all true.

08:11.250 --> 08:14.760
This is the story of a very kind field.

08:15.440 --> 08:19.760
An old woman once lived 
alone in a remote village.

08:20.070 --> 08:24.260
All of a sudden, there was a 
soul dwelling in her field.

08:24.840 --> 08:28.450
That person had come from 
another world, but as a field,

08:28.450 --> 08:30.020
he had no means of speaking.

08:30.020 --> 08:32.600
Day after day, the old 
woman would cultivate him.

08:32.600 --> 08:36.020
<i>A soul inhabiting a field? </i>That's<i> weird.</i>

08:36.020 --> 08:39.110
<i>Well, I guess a soul inside a vending 
machine has no room to talk.</i>

08:39.110 --> 08:42.790
<i>Also, coming from another world means 
it's the same situation as mine.</i>

08:42.790 --> 08:47.540
One day the old woman passed away, 
and the field was left all alone.

08:47.540 --> 08:51.560
However, even a field like him managed 
to make some animal friends.

08:51.560 --> 08:54.220
<i>By "animal," does she 
mean Kuroyata and Botan?</i>

08:54.670 --> 08:57.810
He spent many quiet days with the animals,

08:57.810 --> 09:00.830
until one day, a girl came fleeing.

09:00.830 --> 09:04.310
The field took pity on her, and rescued her.

09:04.570 --> 09:08.350
In order to save even more people, 
the field went on a journey,

09:08.350 --> 09:10.880
and arrived at a fortified 
city in the north.

09:10.880 --> 09:13.330
<i>This might sound odd coming 
from a vending machine,</i>

09:13.330 --> 09:16.060
<i>but a field going on a journey 
sounds overly unreasonable.</i>

09:16.060 --> 09:20.980
There was a fierce battle going on 
there with the Demon Lord's forces.

09:20.980 --> 09:24.010
The field threw himself into the battle!

09:24.010 --> 09:25.280
<i>Despite being a field.</i>

09:25.280 --> 09:27.980
The field managed to drive 
back the Demon Lord's forces,

09:27.980 --> 09:30.930
earning a temporary time of 
peace for the fortified city.

09:30.930 --> 09:32.470
<i>This field kicks ass.</i>

09:32.470 --> 09:35.580
Then he marched into the 
Demon Lord's stronghold,

09:35.580 --> 09:39.150
and after a fierce battle, once his 
friends had managed to escape,

09:39.150 --> 09:41.140
the field shut down his own consciousness.

09:41.140 --> 09:44.940
<i>If this were about a hero, I might 
find the story inspirational,</i>

09:44.940 --> 09:46.970
<i>but the main character is a field.</i>

09:47.220 --> 09:50.990
<i>Well, given how Kikoyu used 
the term "Piece of Field,"</i>

09:50.990 --> 09:54.240
<i>I can surmise that she and the animals 
were the friends who got away.</i>

09:54.240 --> 09:57.230
We wanted to go see Field,

09:57.550 --> 10:00.540
but we couldn't get past the 
huge wall that's across the road

10:00.540 --> 10:03.230
that leads from the fortified 
city to the Demon Lord's domain.

10:03.480 --> 10:06.220
That's when we heard a rumor.

10:06.220 --> 10:09.970
That the Demon Lord's left-arm 
general is here in this dungeon.

10:10.370 --> 10:14.530
We've come here based on that information.

10:16.540 --> 10:17.640
Boxxo.

10:17.140 --> 10:18.290
Boxxo.

10:17.930 --> 10:20.010
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

10:18.030 --> 10:19.230
Boxxo.

10:21.040 --> 10:23.010
And that's the situation.

10:23.010 --> 10:24.740
Yes, I see.

10:24.740 --> 10:27.220
Which means that even if I 
meet with the Netherlord,

10:27.220 --> 10:30.010
it's unlikely I can get 
him to tell me the way.

10:31.460 --> 10:32.520
They're cooked now.

10:32.520 --> 10:33.560
Here you are.

10:33.900 --> 10:35.630
Thank you.

10:39.460 --> 10:40.900
This is delicious!

10:40.900 --> 10:43.910
It's moist, and the sweetness 
spreads all through your mouth!

10:44.200 --> 10:46.640
I'm glad you like it!

10:46.640 --> 10:51.490
But it isn't one-tenth as good as 
vegetables from Field himself.

10:51.490 --> 10:53.930
Or even worse than that.

10:53.930 --> 10:56.740
<i>They taste over ten times better?
That's impressive!</i>

10:56.740 --> 10:59.000
<i>Oh hey, they've got nothing to drink.</i>

10:59.000 --> 11:01.200
<i>Maybe this will go well with 
roasted sweet potatoes.</i>

11:01.890 --> 11:03.740
Uh, there are floating things.

11:03.740 --> 11:06.450
They're drinks Boxxo dispensed.

11:06.450 --> 11:08.780
You open the lid like so.

11:11.850 --> 11:14.400
Wow, how cold and tasty!

11:14.400 --> 11:16.940
So, Boxxo can serve drinks.

11:17.380 --> 11:19.130
More than just that.

11:19.130 --> 11:23.080
He's a dependable guy who provides 
food and all sorts of goods.

11:23.080 --> 11:26.970
Field was able to produce 
any kind of vegetable.

11:26.970 --> 11:29.630
Boxxo is similar to him after all.

11:29.630 --> 11:32.620
<i>Oh right. There was something 
I really want to ask Kikoyu.</i>

11:32.620 --> 11:36.120
<i>F-r-u-m o-th-er w-or-l-d, too.</i>

11:36.120 --> 11:39.920
Huh? Did you say you also 
come from another world?

11:39.920 --> 11:40.890
<i>Y-ea.</i>

11:41.220 --> 11:45.380
It seems the soul inside 
Boxxo is not of our world.

11:45.920 --> 11:50.040
Then perhaps he's from 
the same place as Field!

11:50.040 --> 11:53.890
If I manage to see him again, you should 
try talking to him about things.

11:53.890 --> 11:56.560
<i>I'd love nothing more than that.</i>

11:56.560 --> 12:00.060
<i>If he's a fellow Japanese, there are 
a ton of things I want to discuss.</i>

12:00.060 --> 12:01.100
<i>Y-ea.</i>

12:03.630 --> 12:07.000
<i>We're traveling with Kikoyu now,</i>

12:07.360 --> 12:09.940
<i>and I get to ride on the cart.</i>

12:13.820 --> 12:16.000
It's getting dark.

12:16.680 --> 12:19.380
Let's camp here for the night.

12:23.520 --> 12:26.400
What are these? They taste delicious!

12:27.900 --> 12:30.280
And so do these round things!

12:30.280 --> 12:32.930
<i>I'm glad she seems to like it, 
but now to seal the deal.</i>

12:33.200 --> 12:36.680
<i>Yes, this is what you need for 
capturing a lady's heart!</i>

12:36.680 --> 12:38.620
<i>Form change!</i>

12:38.730 --> 12:39.900
<b>Family Market</b>

12:39.900 --> 12:41.650
<b>Creamy Pudding
 Yummy Yogurt
 Strawberry Yogurt
 Strawberry Shortcake</b>

12:41.650 --> 12:43.930
Wow, what are these?

12:43.930 --> 12:45.420
<i>S-w-ee-t-s.</i>

12:45.420 --> 12:47.780
<i>All</i> of these are sweets?!

12:51.030 --> 12:52.510
That's great!

12:52.510 --> 12:55.100
I've never had food with 
this texture before!

12:55.100 --> 12:56.540
Next I'll try this.

13:00.140 --> 13:02.460
Delicious!

13:02.860 --> 13:06.200
But if this had been made 
with Field's fruit,

13:06.200 --> 13:08.470
it might be even more 
outrageously good.

13:08.470 --> 13:10.900
<i>Yeah, I'd like to sample that.</i>

13:11.970 --> 13:15.240
Sorry, but might I get something to eat, too?

13:15.240 --> 13:18.270
<i>Sorry, Director, I completely forgot!</i>

13:24.890 --> 13:27.480
Boxxo, what do you think of Kikoyu?

13:27.480 --> 13:29.250
<i>N-igh-s k-i-d.</i>

13:29.250 --> 13:32.440
That she is. She's considerate and smart.

13:32.440 --> 13:35.110
So much so that her mind and 
appearance don't seem to match.

13:35.110 --> 13:39.150
<i>True, you rarely see children her 
age who have such firm character.</i>

13:39.150 --> 13:40.630
<i>More like, they don't exist.</i>

13:40.630 --> 13:43.710
Kikoyu probably isn't a human child.

13:43.710 --> 13:48.380
Her abilities and appearance sound 
more like a different race.

13:48.860 --> 13:50.310
A snow child.

13:50.310 --> 13:51.380
<i>Snow child?</i>

13:51.700 --> 13:53.850
Until a snow child becomes an adult,

13:53.850 --> 13:56.860
they apparently retain the 
form of a six-year-old child.

13:56.860 --> 13:59.400
<i>So, their appearance doesn't 
match their true age.</i>

13:59.400 --> 14:02.420
The snow children have special powers.

14:02.420 --> 14:06.500
There's no end of those who go after them, 
and they're in danger of extinction.

14:06.500 --> 14:09.830
In fact, I thought they 
were already extinct.

14:10.160 --> 14:13.500
<i>Special powers that everyone goes after?</i>

14:13.200 --> 14:15.040
<b><i>Kokuuma Cream of Corn Soup</i></b>

14:14.120 --> 14:18.400
It's said that if you behead a snow 
child on the day it becomes an adult,

14:18.400 --> 14:21.800
they turn into an ice 
statue that never melts.

14:21.800 --> 14:26.660
And that the severed head 
will continue to utter curses,

14:26.660 --> 14:28.560
resulting in regional contamination.

14:28.860 --> 14:31.800
I hear there are entire nations 
that perished that way.

14:31.800 --> 14:35.490
<i>That's a killer power, but what it 
takes to invoke it is too cruel!</i>

14:35.490 --> 14:38.800
<i>Beheading someone to cast a curse 
is a horrible thing to do!</i>

14:39.290 --> 14:41.570
The truth is, that's not the end of it.

14:41.570 --> 14:45.850
The headless ice statue 
becomes a curse remover.

14:45.850 --> 14:49.830
Just place it next to a person, 
and it will remove any curse.

14:50.560 --> 14:52.120
<i>It removes curses?!</i>

14:52.120 --> 14:53.320
<i>That means...</i>

14:53.320 --> 14:54.780
<i>C-a-p-t-in.</i>

14:54.780 --> 14:58.830
Yes, it could probably also 
remove Kerioyl's son's curse.

14:58.830 --> 15:01.840
<i>Oh man... If the captain knew about this...</i>

15:01.840 --> 15:05.570
Which is why we'll keep 
this secret to ourselves.

15:05.570 --> 15:07.360
Mum's the word, please.

15:07.360 --> 15:08.600
<i>Y-ea.</i>

15:08.870 --> 15:12.780
<i>No matter what the reason, we can't 
let this girl end up a victim.</i>

15:19.800 --> 15:21.360
<i>Oh, that's a...</i>

15:21.850 --> 15:27.230
It's a magic stone, but I don't know if 
it will get the transfer circle running.

15:27.230 --> 15:28.510
<i>Oh, right.</i>

15:28.510 --> 15:32.120
<i>Without Hulemy, we don't know how much 
we need in terms of magic stones.</i>

15:32.370 --> 15:35.030
Sorry, but let's head back for now.

15:39.010 --> 15:41.420
Looks like I can't pass through after all.

15:41.420 --> 15:46.380
I also tried previously, but there's no 
way to get the Piece of Field through.

15:46.630 --> 15:51.190
I heard this barrier detects monster 
wavelengths, and prevents them from passing.

15:51.190 --> 15:54.530
I'd wager it can't pass 
because it absorbed monsters

15:54.530 --> 15:56.770
and soaked up their wavelengths.

15:56.770 --> 15:58.600
I see.

15:58.600 --> 16:02.140
But I can't leave Field behind here 
and assume nothing bad will happen.

16:03.470 --> 16:05.920
Then let's give something a try.

16:07.470 --> 16:09.770
Kikoyu, cross over to this side.

16:13.480 --> 16:15.320
I-It worked!

16:15.320 --> 16:20.020
Good. Boxxo's barrier successfully 
interrupted the labyrinth's barrier.

16:20.020 --> 16:23.320
Once again, nice to meet you, 
Kikoyu, Kuroyata, Botan.

16:23.580 --> 16:26.290
Thank you very much, Hulemy.

16:28.470 --> 16:33.470
<i>We're back to square one, but we made 
some dependable friends, so that's good.</i>

16:33.830 --> 16:35.030
Director Bear.

16:35.030 --> 16:39.020
I'm done adjusting the transfer circle, 
so I can go with you next time.

16:39.020 --> 16:41.320
That would be reassuring.

16:41.320 --> 16:42.850
<i>Hello there.</i>

16:44.340 --> 16:49.510
<i>We spent the night at an inn,
then entered the maze once again.</i>

16:50.350 --> 16:54.130
<i>And we arrived at the conclusion that, 
rather than do an exhaustive search,</i>

16:54.130 --> 16:59.350
<i>we should try to defeat the dangerous lava 
fiend monster and get its magic stone.</i>

17:00.030 --> 17:01.630
<i>The lava fiend...</i>

17:01.630 --> 17:05.260
<i>It's more dangerous than a stratum lord,
but both Hulemy and Director Bear</i>

17:05.260 --> 17:07.870
<i>thought we'd be fine with this party.</i>

17:07.870 --> 17:11.850
Then shall I have Kuroyata 
search for the lava fiend?

17:11.850 --> 17:13.060
Would you mind?

17:13.060 --> 17:13.910
Not at all.

17:13.910 --> 17:15.890
Kuroyata, would you please do it?

17:18.750 --> 17:21.010
We might as well end the search for today,

17:21.010 --> 17:23.140
and start setting up camp.

17:23.140 --> 17:23.980
Sure.

17:23.980 --> 17:27.150
So, which of you is in 
charge of dinner today?

17:27.150 --> 17:31.140
Boxxo was in charge yesterday, 
so today I will do it!

17:31.140 --> 17:33.220
<i>I c-an d-o i-t.</i>

17:33.220 --> 17:35.850
Oh no, you take it easy today.

17:35.850 --> 17:39.490
Fresh vegetables are good for your 
skin and disease prevention.

17:39.490 --> 17:41.280
<i>I d-o s-w-ee-t-s, too.</i>

17:41.280 --> 17:42.720
Sweets?!

17:43.130 --> 17:46.710
<i>Apparently Hulemy craves sweet 
things after she thinks a lot,</i>

17:46.710 --> 17:49.350
<i>and her secret favorite 
foods are all sugary.</i>

17:51.130 --> 17:55.700
<i>Director Bear sounds noncommittal,
but I know what my regulars' faves are!</i>

17:55.840 --> 17:57.130
<b>Family Market</b>

17:57.510 --> 17:59.220
<i>Bears gotta have their salmon!</i>

17:59.220 --> 18:02.710
<i>Let's see if he can resist this 
veritable salmon torrent!</i>

18:03.400 --> 18:04.860
Wh-Wh-What's this?!

18:05.450 --> 18:08.300
Why don't we go with Boxxo's goods today?

18:08.300 --> 18:10.890
Yeah, let's. I've got no objection.

18:10.890 --> 18:13.160
No fair, Boxxo!

18:13.160 --> 18:15.790
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>

18:15.790 --> 18:16.930
Really!

18:20.550 --> 18:23.010
<i>With the sweet taste of yesterday's 
victory still fresh,</i>

18:23.010 --> 18:25.360
<i>I got some sleep last 
night—a rarity for me.</i>

18:25.720 --> 18:29.050
<i>Kikoyu stood watch from late 
night until early morning,</i>

18:29.050 --> 18:31.220
<i>so I was able to sleep soundly.</i>

18:31.900 --> 18:34.860
<i>Now, I'd better start preparing breakfast...</i>

18:34.860 --> 18:36.970
Good morning, Boxxo!

18:36.970 --> 18:39.430
I made some soup that's 
loaded with vegetables.

18:39.430 --> 18:40.870
<i>She got me!</i>

18:40.870 --> 18:43.050
<i>This was her scheme the whole time!</i>

18:44.870 --> 18:46.350
I-It's good.

18:46.350 --> 18:49.470
That tender flavor seeps all through me!

18:50.610 --> 18:52.620
Welcome back, Kuroyata.

18:53.610 --> 18:55.340
Okay, thank you.

18:55.340 --> 18:58.060
It seems Kuroyata has found the lava fiend.

18:58.570 --> 19:03.320
If we know where it is, I have a good 
idea of how to beat that lava fiend.

19:05.300 --> 19:07.370
<i>It should be around here.</i>

19:07.370 --> 19:07.870
<i>Oh?</i>

19:11.460 --> 19:14.110
<i>There it goes now.</i>

19:15.870 --> 19:20.380
<i>And that's a wall I built 
using concrete slabs.</i>

19:20.380 --> 19:22.880
<i>And I actually built two walls!</i>

19:22.880 --> 19:25.140
<i>Why did I do such a thing, you ask?</i>

19:26.700 --> 19:30.380
<i>You go have lots of fun 
in that ice water now!</i>

19:30.890 --> 19:35.260
<i>Being doused with that much icy-cold 
water will chill even you.</i>

19:36.070 --> 19:39.600
<i>That might have only hardened your outside,
but that's good enough!</i>

19:42.310 --> 19:46.210
<i>According to Hulemy, the lava 
fiend's weak point is its throat!</i>

19:48.700 --> 19:51.760
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

19:56.880 --> 19:59.000
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>

20:02.160 --> 20:03.700
<i>Huh? It regenerated?!</i>

20:03.700 --> 20:05.000
<i>Uh oh!</i>

20:06.270 --> 20:07.520
<i>Wh-What's that?</i>

20:12.150 --> 20:13.780
<i>Th-That was...</i>

20:13.780 --> 20:16.390
<i>No way, a stratum split?!</i>

20:16.390 --> 20:17.900
<i>And for that matter, that's...</i>

20:18.510 --> 20:20.160
<i>Lammis!</i>

20:20.410 --> 20:24.160
That doofus helped herself to my inventions.

20:24.160 --> 20:26.870
Boxxo!

20:28.390 --> 20:31.230
Boxxo, you're okay!

20:31.230 --> 20:32.530
Who's this bird?

20:32.530 --> 20:34.150
<i>A f-r-e-n-d.</i>

20:34.860 --> 20:37.530
I'm glad I found you!

20:37.530 --> 20:38.440
<i>Bad.</i>

20:38.440 --> 20:40.500
Boxxo, are you angry?

20:40.500 --> 20:43.430
<i>Y-ea. F-your-i-o-s.</i>

20:43.430 --> 20:44.460
What?!

20:44.460 --> 20:46.430
N-No, Boxxo!

20:46.430 --> 20:49.300
<i>That was reckless. You could 
have died if it went wrong.</i>

20:49.300 --> 20:52.310
If you've got an explanation, 
we'd like to hear it, too.

20:52.310 --> 20:55.820
W-Wait, shouldn't this be where 
we're happy to see each other?

20:55.820 --> 20:58.340
Lammis. Tell us what happened since then,

20:58.340 --> 21:00.950
and how you came to fall out of the sky.

21:00.950 --> 21:04.150
Well you see, Director Origin and I

21:04.150 --> 21:07.780
were lucky enough to transfer 
to Clearflow Lake stratum.

21:07.780 --> 21:10.960
I remembered how Director Bear said

21:10.960 --> 21:14.320
if you cause an impact on a stratum split,
 it might split again.

21:14.320 --> 21:18.430
And then, Hulemy's magic item that 
lets you safely drop from high up,

21:18.430 --> 21:21.520
and the one that freezes water 
were there, so I used 'em!

21:21.520 --> 21:22.960
I'm sorry!

21:22.960 --> 21:26.170
And so, when I punched the 
frozen pond with all my might,

21:26.170 --> 21:29.220
the stratum split again, 
I fell head over heels...

21:29.220 --> 21:30.940
and now here I am.

21:32.520 --> 21:35.340
<i>That </i>would<i> make you want to sigh deeply!</i>

21:35.340 --> 21:37.100
<i>It's just too darn impulsive.</i>

21:37.410 --> 21:41.980
Lammis, what were you going to do if 
we weren't in the Labyrinth stratum?

21:42.260 --> 21:45.710
Well, I just had a feeling you were here.

21:45.710 --> 21:47.480
<i>The ultimate hunch!</i>

21:47.480 --> 21:50.130
The most important thing 
is you're safe, Lammis.

21:50.130 --> 21:54.890
I just want you to realize we're 
all angry out of concern for you.

21:54.890 --> 21:58.500
Yeah. I'm sorry to worry you all.

21:58.500 --> 22:01.490
So, I'm happy we're safely 
back together, Lammis.

22:02.320 --> 22:04.640
I'm back, everybody!

23:35.060 --> 23:37.070
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>The Dark Forest Stratum</b>

23:37.930 --> 23:40.100
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
